hadiths[22]{hadithnumber,text}:
"484","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""‘Umra (gifting something to someone for the duration of his life) is inheritance for his heirs. Or it is permissible for his heirs."""
"485","Shurayh narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) gave a verdict regarding 'Umra that it is permissible."
"486","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Umra is permissible."""
"487","Qatadah (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated, Hasan (may Allah have mercy on him) said: They used to say: ‘Umrah is permissible.’"
"488","Imam Zuhri, may Allah have mercy on him, said: 'Umra is that a person says: ""This is for him, and after him for his offspring."" So it is for the one for whom he sets the condition.'"
"489","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Umra is permissible."""
"490","Imam Zuhri, may Allah have mercy on him, said: The caliphs used to decide this matter. Ata, may Allah have mercy on him, said: Abdul Malik bin Marwan decided this matter."
"491","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Umra is permissible."""
"492","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever is given something without asking for it and he accepts it, then it is a provision that Allah has sent to him."""
"493","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""If I am given the gift of a foreleg, I will accept it, and if I am invited to a meal of a foot, I will also accept that invitation."""
"494","A’mash, may Allah have mercy on him, narrated with this chain a narration similar to the previous hadith."
"495","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""If I am given the gift of the meat of the foreleg, I will accept it."" Jarir (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated: I think that he (peace be upon him) said: ""If I am invited to the meat of the foreleg, I will accept it."""
"496","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""The one who takes back his gift is like a dog that keeps eating until it is full, then vomits, and then starts eating its vomit."""
"497","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: When food was presented to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in a house other than his own, he would ask: ""Is this a gift or charity?"" If it was said that it was charity, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would not eat from it, but his companions would eat it. And if it was said that it was a gift, then he (peace and blessings be upon him) would eat from it."
"498","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""The one who takes back his gift is like a dog that vomits and then licks it up."""
"499","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""The one who takes back his gift is like a dog who vomits and then licks it up."""
"500","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not lawful for anyone to give a gift and then take it back, except for a father who gives something to his child. The example of a person who gives a gift and then takes it back is like a dog who vomits and then licks it up."""
"501","Tawoos (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not lawful for anyone to give a gift and then take it back, except for a father (he may take back what he has given to his child)."""
"502","Ata (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who takes back his gift is like the one who licks up his own vomit."""
"503","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""When a gift is given to any one of you and there are some people present with him, then they also share in it."""
"504","Narrated by Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""There is no bad example for us (we will not be among those described by this example); the one who takes back his gift is like a dog that vomits and then licks it up."""
"505","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) a narration similar to the previous hadith."
